This version of SET has the SET HANDLER old=new option; unlike DEC's version
however, it will work on ALL systems, regardless of whether they have 1-page
or 2-page system handlers and whether or not the hardware can do a BSW!  The
purpose of the SET HANDLER feature is to allow one to easily reconfigure the
system without having to run BUILD.   This allows seldom-used handlers to be
installed only when they are needed, freeing up scarce system space for fre-
quently used devices such as large disks.  The symbols 'old' and 'new' refer
to files on SYS that contain SAVED versions of the handlers; a .HN extension
is required.  The 'old' handler must already be installed, and must be for a
different device than the 'new' handler, but the number of entry points need
not be the same (provided there is space in the 'name' table); handlers with
different lengths can also be interchanged.  The '/L' option can be used for
listing SOME of the handlers available, but a '.RESORC/E' listing is better.

Command	=	.SET device [NO] option [= value]

Device	=	TTY:	SLU2:	SLU3:	VLU2:	VLU3:
Options	=	ARROW	CODE	COL	ECHO	ESC	FILL	FLAG
		HEIGTH	LC	PAGE	PAUSE	SCOPE	TAB	WIDTH

Device	=	LPT:
Options	=	LC	LA78	LA8A	LV8E	WIDTH

Device	=	MTA0:
Options	=	PARITY EVEN/ODD

Device	=	CDR:
Options	=	CODE

Device	=	SYS:
Options	=	OS8	OS78	INIT xxxxx (5 char command string)

Device	=	any
Options =	BLOCK	DVC	FILES	LOC    VERSION    READONLY
